sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/levin-2023-agential-19> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "The multiscale competency architecture smooths the fitness landscape by reducing phenotypic differences between genotypes, letting evolution explore mutations that would otherwise be lethal (e.g. a mutation that displaces the mouth but has another benefit survives because the mouth self-corrects), which makes search more efficient and helps it overcome local maxima.";
    dc:type "mechanism";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Multiscale competency smooths the fitness landscape and lets search escape local maxima";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Levin M, “Darwin's agential materials: evolutionary implications of multiscale competency in developmental biology”, Cellular and molecular life sciences : CMLS (2023), doi:10.1007/s00018-023-04790-z; section “Implications of multiscale competency for the evolutionary process”. Scope: Evolution of organisms with regulative development"
}
